source: tests/ui/lint/mod.rs
---
  ● Redundant `strings.HasPrefix` guard
    ╭─[test.lis:7:3]
  6 │       let mut out = "www.example.com"
  7 │ ╭─▶   if strings.HasPrefix(out, affix) {
  8 │ │       out = strings.TrimPrefix(out, affix)
  9 │ ├─▶   }
    · ╰──── can be simpler
 10 │       let _ = out
    ╰────
  help: `strings.TrimPrefix` already returns the string unchanged when the prefix is absent. Replace the `if` with `out = strings.TrimPrefix(out, affix)` · code: [lint.redundant_trim_guard]
